// TEST: A static function's applied parameter takes an array or a function at run time
// ============================================================================
// A `static function` is also emitted for run-time calls, and its arrow
// parameter is decided per call like any declaration's: an array call is a
// call of its array instance, a function call a call of it.
static function first(c) = c(0) + 1.0
let v = [1.0, 2.0]
let a = first(v)
// EXPECT: a = 2
let b = first(lambda(i) -> Float64(i) + 3.0)
// EXPECT: b = 4
